glsl/meson: look up SPIRV through the default library search

Search for SPIRV without the static:/dirs: restrictions so it is found
from the MacPorts prefix.

Rebased ppcports libplacebo-spirv.patch onto v7.387.0. Its first hunk,
which added libglslang to the dependency list up front, is dropped: the
build now links libglslang right after SPIRV is found (the "Glslang
15.0.0 moved some code around" step in src/glsl/meson.build), so the
extra entry was redundant. Only the +glslang variant uses this file.

diff --git a/src/glsl/meson.build b/src/glsl/meson.build
index c9a85429..c9584878 100644
--- a/src/glsl/meson.build
+++ b/src/glsl/meson.build
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ elif not glslang_req.disabled()
     static   = arg[0]
     required = arg[1]
 
-    spirv = cxx.find_library('SPIRV', required: required, static: static, dirs: vulkan_lib_dirs)
+    spirv = cxx.find_library('SPIRV', required: required)
 
     if not spirv.found()
       continue
